Spec: InstanceTenant

Purpose:
  Be the @TenantInstance implementation of the shared reconcile engine: fix the tenant kind's
    identity literals (`tenant`, its finalizer, the Tenant package type), forward the
    macro-attached accessors and status setters to the CR model, run the tenant-side requirement
    evaluator @VynilPackageRequirement::check_tenant, override the engine's init-version pair
    (the tenant has the `InitFrom` stage), fill the one recommendation lane no sibling uses —
    filtering @VynilPackageRecommandation::TenantService entries against @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names
    — feed the two tenant metric slots, delegate @Reconciler to @do_reconcile/@do_cleanup, and
    own the controller entry pair @reconcile/@error_policy that ./manager.rs wires on the
    @TenantInstance watch, including this kind's consumption of the 30-second
    @Error::CleanupInProgress transient lane and the 5-minute counted-failure lane.

References:
  ./instance_common.sdd — @InstanceKind engine whose implementation this is: every method here
    is bound by that contract (supertraits, the seventeen required methods, the two defaults this
    kind overrides, the discard-the-returned-@Self setter lanes, the verbatim
    @InstanceKind::check_requirements action pass-through, engine-owned stages and durations);
    @RecoContext, @run_with_finalizer, @do_reconcile, @do_cleanup and
    @build_base_recommendations all run from there.
  ./lib.sdd — @Reconciler implemented here per its Must; crate-root re-exported
    @TenantInstance, @Error and @Result are the names this file imports through @crate.
  ./manager.sdd — @Context (its @metrics field is the only @Context member read here) and the
    @Controller::@run wiring that pairs this file's @instancetenant::@reconcile with
    @instancetenant::@error_policy on an @any_semantic cluster-wide watch; the @TenantInstance
    CRD probe is @Manager::new's second.
  ./metrics.sdd — @Metrics::tenant_instance, the @count_and_measure runs increment with the five
    @LabelInstance labels, @reconcile_failure's single six-label increment and the
    @ReconcileMeasurerInstance; that spec confirms the tenant lane is live from this file's
    call sites.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the @TenantInstance CRD model this file attaches to (that
    spec sits in the common crate under the same basename as this spec: it owns the type, the
    @TenantInstance::have_child probe, @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names and the
    macro-attached method set; this spec owns only the operator-side @crate impls and entry fns
    co-named in ./instancetenant.rs).
  /common/src/instance_macros.sdd — the mutator contract the forwarding methods pass through
    unchanged (@TenantInstance::get_options_digest, @TenantInstance::set_missing_box,
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_package, @TenantInstance::set_missing_requirement,
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_init_version and the server-side patch/condition semantics
    behind them).
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackageType::Tenant,
    @VynilPackageRecommandation::TenantService and the @VynilPackageRequirement::check_tenant
    evaluator, including its tenant-specific arms (`TenantPackage`, `TenantService`), its
    per-arm ttl seconds and the always-satisfied catch-all arm.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script whose @ctx receives the instance binding.

Must:
  Implement @InstanceKind for @TenantInstance under @async_trait, overriding both engine
    defaults: @InstanceKind::init_from_version and @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version are
    real tenant-lane methods, not the @None/@Ok(self) defaults (the service kind overrides the
    same pair; @SystemInstance has no `initFrom` and keeps the defaults).
  Fix the three identity literals: @InstanceKind::type_name answers exactly `tenant` (pinning,
    through the engine, the `tenant--<namespace>--<name>` Job name and the `package_type` render
    key), @InstanceKind::finalizer_name answers exactly `tenantinstances.vynil.solidite.fr` (the
    string kube adds on apply and removes after a @Ok cleanup), and @InstanceKind::package_type
    answers @VynilPackageType::Tenant (the cache-lookup type clause).
  Borrow @TenantInstanceSpec::jukebox, @TenantInstanceSpec::category and
    @TenantInstanceSpec::package verbatim from @InstanceKind::spec_jukebox,
    @InstanceKind::spec_category and @InstanceKind::spec_package.
  Gate install state in @InstanceKind::current_tag: `status.tag` clone when both the status and
    the tag are present, the empty @String through @unwrap_or_default otherwise;
    @InstanceKind::init_from_version answers the @Option<@InitFrom>::version borrow — @None when
    `initFrom` is absent or its `version` is @None.
  Forward, unmodified, the model-owned methods: @InstanceKind::have_child calls the inherent
    @TenantInstance::have_child — Rust resolves the same-name call to the inherent probe, not
    recursively to the trait method; @InstanceKind::get_options_digest passes the `&mut self`
    receiver to the macro digest; the four setters @InstanceKind::set_missing_box,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_package, @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement and
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version call their macro counterparts on the moved copy's
    @&mut self and hand back the macro's @Result<Self> unchanged (the tenant setter writes the
    `InitFrom` stage condition owned by /common/src/instancetenant.sdd).
  Run @InstanceKind::check_requirements as an in-order scan over the requirement list with the
    moved @Client cloned per call: on the first @VynilPackageRequirement::check_tenant verdict
    with a false outcome, record the message via @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement on a
    clone of self (its returned @Self discarded) and return @Some(@Action::requeue(
    @tokio::time::@Duration::from_secs(ttl))) carrying that arm's ttl literal; evaluation @Err
    propagates through `?` with no condition recorded; an all-true list answers @None.
  Build @InstanceKind::build_recommendations as the tenant-only lane (the service and system
    kinds purely delegate and leave @RecoContext::tenant_services empty): first await
    @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names on self — an unconditional tenant-namespace
    cluster read that runs before the recommendation list is inspected, whose @Err aborts the
    whole reco stage — even when `recos` is @None or empty.
  Partition the recos (@None taken as the empty list) on the
    @VynilPackageRecommandation::TenantService variant via @matches!: keep one
    @RecoContext::tenant_services entry per matching reco occurrence whose name the fetched list
    contains (repeated recos repeat the entry; no dedup of the kept names), silently drop
    tenant-service recos the tenant does not currently publish, then sort the kept list.
  Always call @build_base_recommendations with @Some of the non-tenant residue — even when the
    incoming `recos` was @None, which reaches the base lane as @Some of an empty list and still
    pays its full service-index fetch — and return @RecoContext carrying the base pair plus the
    sorted tenant list; the crds/system-services filtering and sorting stay engine-owned.
  Bind, in @InstanceKind::set_rhai_instance, the cloned @TenantInstance onto @Script::ctx under
    the key `instance`, so value scripts see the type registered by @tenant_rhai_register of
    /common/src/instancetenant.sdd.
  Wire both metric slots to @Metrics::tenant_instance: @InstanceKind::count_and_measure_metrics
    forwards to its @count_and_measure, @InstanceKind::record_reconcile_failure to its
    @reconcile_failure; this file adds no label of its own, and no other tenant metric call site
    exists in it — the exemplar lane and the transient-lane failure skip come from ./metrics.sdd
    and @error_policy below.
  Delegate @Reconciler wholly to the engine — @Reconciler::reconcile @Box::pins @do_reconcile
    and @Reconciler::cleanup @Box::pins @do_cleanup on `&self` with the @Arc<@Context> moved in,
    no tenant-specific step between; the `# Errors` doc on each names the engine as the error
    source.
  Instrument @reconcile `#[instrument(skip(ctx, inst), fields(trace_id))]` — the attribute sits
    above the fn's doc comment — the span carrying a declared-empty `trace_id` field (the engine
    of ./instance_common.sdd records the same name on the current @Span), hiding both arguments;
    its body is exactly @Box::pin(@run_with_finalizer(inst, ctx)).await with @Ok/@Err passed
    through.
  Split failure handling in @error_policy on @Error::CleanupInProgress as the first test: that
    arm discards its @Job payload and answers @Action::requeue(@Duration::from_secs(30)) with no
    log line, no metric and no @tracing::@warn!; every other @Error answers
    @Action::requeue(@Duration::from_mins(5)) after the @tracing::@warn! line and exactly one
    @InstanceKind::record_reconcile_failure increment, and is matched by nothing else.

Must not:
  Drive agent-side stage flow: no call here touches the tenant `ScheduleBackup`/backup or
    children-stage setters — the only condition this file can write is the missing-requirement
    or missing-box/package one the engine or @check_tenant asks the forwarded setters to record;
    backup and schedule stages belong to scripts on /common/src/instancetenant.sdd.

Exposes:
  @reconcile — `#[instrument] pub async fn @reconcile(inst: @Arc<@TenantInstance>, ctx:
    @Arc<@Context>) -> @Result<@Action>`; the controller entry for the @TenantInstance watch.
  @error_policy — `#[must_use] pub fn @error_policy(inst: @Arc<@TenantInstance>, error:
    &@Error, ctx: @Arc<@Context>) -> @Action`; consumes both @Arcs by value, borrows the error.
  @InstanceKind for @TenantInstance — `#[async_trait]` impl, surface and literals per Must.
  @Reconciler for @TenantInstance — `#[async_trait]` impl delegating to @do_reconcile and
    @do_cleanup.

Accepts:
  A watch-event-carried @TenantInstance of any shape: `spec` strings unvalidated, `status`
    @Option read opportunistically (@current_tag and @init_from_version never fail on absence),
    a requirement list of any length or emptiness (empty answers @None without a single call),
    and recos whose @None arm still costs this kind two cluster reads (see Must).
  @error_policy accepts the @Arcs moved — nothing reads them after the metric call (the trailing
    @drop calls are explicit no-ops on already-unused owners) — and any @Error variant, the
    @Error::CleanupInProgress arm discriminating on the variant only, payload ignored.

Returns:
  @reconcile returns the @Action the engine pipeline produced for the tenant kind (15-minute
    requeues, ttl requeues via the pass-through, @Action::await_change() releases) and @Err the
    engine's errors — nothing here maps an @Err into an @Action.
  @error_policy returns exactly one of two requeues: @Duration::from_secs(30) on the transient
    cleanup arm, @Duration::from_mins(5) on everything else.
  @InstanceKind::check_requirements returns @None or the single short-circuit @Some requeue;
    @InstanceKind::build_recommendations a @RecoContext whose @RecoContext::tenant_services is
    sorted and may be non-empty; @InstanceKind::count_and_measure_metrics the started
    @ReconcileMeasurerInstance.

Raises:
  None of its own: every fallible body forwards. @InstanceKind::set_missing_box,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_package, @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version, @InstanceKind::check_requirements (through
    @VynilPackageRequirement::check_tenant and the condition write),
    @InstanceKind::build_recommendations (through @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names —
    @Error::KubeError or the no-namespace @Error::Other of /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — and
    the base lane) and both @Reconciler methods propagate model, requirement or engine @Error
    variants — the engine variant set belongs to ./instance_common.sdd.
  @reconcile surfaces the same engine @Err, dominated by @Error::FinalizerError on wrapper
    failures; @error_policy is total and @Action-valued, and raises nothing in either arm.

Handles:
  A delete Job still running (@Error::CleanupInProgress) — the expected-transient 30-second
    lane: fast requeue, finalizer retained by the wrapper, runs already counted but no failure
    increment; this file is one of three consumers of that engine variant.
  Every other reconcile failure — one @tracing::@warn! naming kind, namespace and name, one
    failures-series increment on `tenant_instance_reconcile_failures_total`, then the 5-minute
    backoff; the warn @Debug-formats the @Option metadata, so absent-vs-present namespace reads
    `Some("apps")` vs @None inside the message (Tasks `[?]`).
  An unmet requirement — condition recorded on a discarded clone, only its ttl drives the
    requeue, later requirements unevaluated; a requirement variant the tenant lane's catch-all
    arm pronounces satisfied never reaches the condition write.
  A `status`-less tenant during selection gates — empty tag and @None init version are plain
    answers, not errors.
  A TenantService reco naming a service the tenant does not currently publish — silently dropped
    from @RecoContext::tenant_services, no condition, no error, the pass continues.
  A failing @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names read — aborts @do_reconcile at the reco
    stage as @Err even when no TenantService reco exists.

Depends on:
  ./instance_common.rs — @InstanceKind, @RecoContext, @build_base_recommendations,
    @run_with_finalizer, @do_reconcile, @do_cleanup.
  ./manager.rs — @Context; read through the trait signatures, only @Context::metrics touched.
  ./metrics.rs paths — @ReconcileMeasurerInstance named in the trait surface; the
    @ReconcileMetricsTenantInstance methods run there.
  @common — @rhaihandler::@Script, @vynilpackage::@VynilPackageRecommandation,
    @VynilPackageRequirement and @VynilPackageType via the crate-root @TenantInstance re-export;
    @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names reaches the cluster on its own common-lane client.
  @kube — @Client (cloned per requirement check), @kube::runtime::controller::@Action.
  @tokio::time::@Duration, @opentelemetry::trace::@TraceId, @tracing (@instrument, @warn),
    @async_trait, @std::sync::@Arc.

Tasks:
  [ ] No test covers this file directly: no in-file @cfg(test) module exists. Only the
      ./instance_common.rs tests touch its lanes indirectly —
      @test_init_from_version_tenant_with_version and @test_init_from_version_tenant_no_init_from
      call @InstanceKind::init_from_version on a built @TenantInstance, and
      @test_resolve_init_version_no_version / @test_resolve_init_version_already_installed /
      @test_resolve_init_version_found_in_cache plus the @test_do_reconcile_tag_* documentation
      tests drive the tenant selectors through @resolve_init_version, never @do_reconcile.
      Cover the rest from the Scenarios — kind literals, forwarding, requirement-scan short
      circuit, reco partition/filter/sort and its reads, both @error_policy lanes, entry
      delegation — per TTD, reusing the ./instance_common.rs @make_tenant style.
  [x] ./metrics.sdd contradicted this file: its Must claimed "no call site invokes the tenant
      @reconcile_failure or @count_and_measure" and its Scenario froze the tenant registry at
      zero, yet this impl wires both slots to @Metrics::tenant_instance (./instancetenant.rs
      @reconcile and @error_policy sites) and the engine binds
      @InstanceKind::count_and_measure_metrics for every kind's reconcile
      (./instance_common.sdd). Resolved: ./metrics.sdd corrected — its Must now states all four
      kind registries serve live call sites, the zero-scenario replaced by an all-kinds-children
      scenario, and the `[?]` half-wired entry deleted.
  [?] @InstanceKind::build_recommendations fetches @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names
      unconditionally and hands @build_base_recommendations a forced @Some, so a tenant whose
      package declares no recommendations at all still pays two cluster reads per pass (the
      tenant-namespace service scan plus the base lane's service index) where service and system
      pay none on @None. Decide whether the tenant lane gates on @Some (and forwards the original
      @Option) instead.
  [?] @error_policy warn reads `reconcile failed for TenantInstance '{:?}.{:?}': {:?}` with
      namespace before name and @Debug on both @Option metadata fields, so shipped lines render
      `Some("apps").Some("frontend")`; the trailing @drop(inst)/@drop(ctx) are no-ops that only
      appease move analysis; @reconcile's `#[instrument]` sits above its doc comment; and
      @error_policy takes @Arcs by value though only borrows are used — cosmetic-only drift, the
      same findings filed `[?]` in ./instanceservice.sdd. Decide entry-fn style once for all
      three kinds.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a green mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, the ./metrics.sdd idle-lane
    contradiction is resolved in that spec, and `cargo test -p operator`,
    `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and
    `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: Kind literals pin the tenant identity
  Given any @TenantInstance
  When @InstanceKind::type_name, @InstanceKind::finalizer_name and @InstanceKind::package_type
    answer
  Then they are exactly `tenant`, `tenantinstances.vynil.solidite.fr` and
    @VynilPackageType::Tenant — so the engine names the agent Job `tenant--<ns>--<name>` and the
    cache lookup matches only Tenant-type packages
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Tag and initFrom read the status gates
  Given four tenants — no status, status without `tag`, installed `tag` `1.2.3`, and a fresh one
    whose `spec.initFrom.version` is `0.9.0`
  When @InstanceKind::current_tag and @InstanceKind::init_from_version run
  Then the first two answer the empty @String, the third answers `1.2.3` regardless of initFrom
    (the engine ignores the pin once installed), and @InstanceKind::init_from_version answers
    @Some(`0.9.0`) only for the fourth, @None whenever `initFrom` is absent or its `version` is
    @None — the tenant override, not the engine default
  Maps to tests @test_init_from_version_tenant_with_version and
    @test_init_from_version_tenant_no_init_from; the installed-tag arm is driven indirectly by
    @test_resolve_init_version_already_installed

Scenario: First unmet tenant requirement short-circuits on its own ttl
  Given a requirement list whose second @VynilPackageRequirement fails @check_tenant with the
    ttl of its arm
  When @InstanceKind::check_requirements scans with a @Client
  Then the evaluator's message is stored via @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement and the
    answer is @Some(@Action::requeue(ttl)) — the third requirement is never evaluated
  But an all-satisfied list answers @None with zero condition writes, and an evaluator @Err
    propagates with no condition written
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Recommendations keep only the tenant's live services
  Given recos naming one installed CRD and TenantService entries `web` (published by the tenant
    per @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names) and `gone` (not published)
  When @InstanceKind::build_recommendations runs with @Some recos
  Then @RecoContext carries the base-filtered sorted `crds` (plus `system_services`), and
    @tenant_services is exactly the kept `web` — repeats when the reco list repeats a live name —
    `gone` silently dropped
  But with @None recos the tenant service scan and the base service-index fetch still happen,
    both lists answer empty (Tasks `[?]`)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: CleanupInProgress requeues fast and uncounted
  Given @error_policy met with @Error::CleanupInProgress carrying a @Job
  When it runs
  Then the answer is @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::@Duration::from_secs(30)), no
    @tracing::@warn! line is written and the failures counter does not move
  But met with any other @Error it warns once, increments
    `tenant_instance_reconcile_failures_total` under the six labels of ./metrics.sdd exactly
    once, and answers @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::@Duration::from_mins(5))
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Entry pair delegates with no local decision
  Given a @TenantInstance handed to @reconcile
  When the call resolves
  Then exactly @run_with_finalizer ran — dispatching @Reconciler::reconcile, which runs
    @do_reconcile, and @Reconciler::cleanup, which runs @do_cleanup — the whole pipeline body
    belonging to ./instance_common.sdd, this file contributing only literals, the reco tenant
    lane, metric forwards and forwards
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  error_policy input/output pairs: @Error::CleanupInProgress(@Job) → requeue `30` s silent;
    @Error::Other("E_X") → warn + one failure inc + requeue `5` min.
  check_requirements on [ok, fail(ttl 900)] @Ok answer: @Some(requeue `900` s) — ttl values
    belong to /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd.
  rec_tenant_services for recos [`web`, `web`, `gone`] with `web` live: @Vec [`web`, `web`].